just making conversation
its not about whether I care, its about what matters to you. You don&apos;t need to go away for 6 months to figure that out from a bunch of bible belt ultraconservative freak shows.
im christian...and idc what they think of me, i just dont wanna be miserable anymore.
how else am i supposed to get better?
people get depressed, and some have it harder than others. I went through a really bad stage in my life as well, and was even hospitalized for it. And I did have it really bad, but literally nothing anyone in there said or did changed my mind about my depression. and i can GUARANTEE no one in there will do it for you. Only you can change your mind about how you feel; and I can give you a good start:
how?
hello?
You first must recognize that some people do have it bad, I mean, your mother ran out. And that&apos;s a terrible thing to have happen: but you know what, no one will fully understand what you&apos;ve gone through. I can&apos;t begin to fathom what that was like, or how I would feel. But I can also tell you that you&apos;ll become a stronger person for it if you let yourself, and above anything and all else in this world, above your Christian God and your forsaken mother, you can be proud of yourself. You CAN BE PROUD OF YOURSELF. You will have done something to take pride in.
And sometimes, that&apos;s what you need to pull yourself out of your slump, you don&apos;t realize that the reason you&apos;re depressed is because you truly think that there&apos;s nothing to be proud of yourself for, but there certainly is if you start making right choices: going to school, getting a CRITICAL THINKING education, saying no to sex, drugs, and violence at your age. Thinking about your future. Honestly, the future is a very dangerous thing to think about, it can be scary, but it can also be inspirational. And you absolutely must focus on the inspirational parts.
Your future is the most important thing that America has right now, and you can be proud of that. America won&apos;t thank you for it, they may never acknowledge your even alive, but I really believe that the best feelings of worthfulness come from inside; the realization that you, yourself, have broken through this barrier, and that you&apos;re going to keep on kicking even if the bubble seems unbreakable. Because as long as you are you, make the right choices, then it doesn&apos;t matter if the rest of the world recognizes you for it, what truly matters is that you recognize yourself for it
thank you. i dont know if ill be able to really get thru it on my own tho...
You won&apos;t get through it at all if you can&apos;t get through it on your own. How can anyone else help you overcome your problems in life when literally no one understands what you&apos;re going through? They&apos;re not you, never will be, will never fully understand the depth and complexities that make you, you. But, that doesn&apos;t mean your helpless, that just makes you stronger for your ability to cope and overcome. You don&apos't have to go away for 6 months to figure out that way."")
