CONVERSATION:
Was there supposed to be a joint XHTML/SVG/WAI meeting today?
tina: i'll try and ping RichS on that -- he was supposed to organize, and i was supposed to participate, but haven't heard anything (although having said that, i should recheck my email)
50fa2422c663a31e707bdd4f9e4ed4c5: I can't find any mention of such a meeting being called.
tina: there is a PFWG meeting at noon NYC time
Is this a f2f meeting?
tina: it has been discussed in both PF and ARIA subteam meetings
Because the details of the meeting being posted on the xhtml mailing list is an irc one.
i think the original plan was to meet virtually and, depending upon who will be at TPAC, meet there -- let me check if RichS is in the #pf channel
nope -- i'm the only one in #pf right now
Would you happen to know the exact date the call for that meeting was posted?
as far as i know it WASN'T posted -- i was supposed to be in on the call, but it appears that it was held on the sly...
Ok. So if I get this correctly ... a joint XHTML, SVG and ARIA meeting was meant to be held virtually, but the XHTML group members were not informed ... ?
i'm confused, as i had been the one to push for a meeting to get rid of the aria- hack so that ARIA works today and tomorrow -- especially in XML-based languages -- that was 2 weeks ago
not only were XHTML WG members not told, neither were PF members -- including those specifically designated to participate
Very interesting.
